      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Deep brain stimulation analgesia is an effective method of treating otherwise intractable chronic pain, with few side-effects, and long-term good or better results in 50% to 80% of patients, depending on etiology and stimulation site. In general, the best results are in deafferentation pain with internal capsule stimulation and somatic pain with periventricular stimulation."},
